# Build-context exclusions for the frontend image.
#
# Build context is ``frontend/`` (see homelabsetup/deploy-homelab.sh:357).
# The biggest exclusions here are ``node_modules`` (rebuilt inside the
# image via ``npm ci``) and ``dist`` (rebuilt by ``npm run build``);
# leaving them in the context pushes hundreds of MB across the docker
# socket and busts every cached layer when ``npm install`` runs on any
# developer's machine.

# ── Node / build outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.cache/
.vite/
.next/

# ── Test artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
tests/e2e/.auth/
tests/.tmp/

# ── Secrets / per-developer config ───────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── IDE / OS clutter ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
*.md

# ── pytest caches / basetemp roots ───────────────────────────────────
# These are permission-locked on Windows, and podman aborts the ENTIRE
# image build reading their extended attributes:
#   copier: get: getting extended attributes for "/.pytest-cache-m10":
#   permission denied
# That failure cost a homelab deploy from backend/, whose ignore covered
# the underscore spelling but not the hyphenated one. Both separators are
# matched here so this context cannot repeat it.
# Every pytest scratch root, whatever the session named it. The three
# spellings below were each added after a build broke on a variant the
# previous pattern missed: `.pytest_cache`, then `.pytest_tmp_*`, then
# `.pytest-cache-m10`. `.pytest_cache_t0` slipped past all three and
# failed the mcp image build on 2026-09-18 with
#   copier: get: getting extended attributes for "/.pytest_cache_t0":
#   permission denied
# (pytest creates these owner-only on Windows, so the context walk cannot
# even stat them). One pattern for the whole class ends the sequence.
.pytest*/
**/.pytest*/
